menu "nRF log collector"

config NRF_LOG_POLL_NODE_BUDGET_MS
    int "Deadline for one node visit, including mux close (ms)"
    range 120 1000
    default 120
    help
        Includes selection, a bounded request/reply, mux close and one scheduler
        tick. Work stops between pairs and resumes from the saved protocol phase.
        The 150 ms bus-owner guard remains independent of this visit budget.

config NRF_LOG_POLL_ITERATION_BUDGET_MS
    int "Deadline for one log polling slice (ms)"
    range 120 2000
    default 120
    help
        Every pair, including the first STATUS or BLOCK, must fit. Remaining
        nodes and protocol progress resume in a later slice. Urgent work stops
        collection at the next safe pair boundary. Driver timeouts are bounded
        by the remaining deadline; task preemption can still delay scheduling.

config NRF_LOG_POLL_PERIOD_MS
    int "Interval between log polling rounds (ms)"
    range 100 60000
    default 1000

config NRF_LOG_POLL_BACKOFF_MAX_ROUNDS
    int "Maximum backoff after a log transport or protocol fault (rounds)"
    range 1 255
    default 32

endmenu
